---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PostTestForm from "@/components/PostTestForm.astro";
export const prerender = true;
---
<BaseLayout title="HTTP Post Test" description="Submit text and files over HTTP to a safe endpoint that immediately discards them. Use it to verify your DLP can block sensitive data in transit.">
  <h1>HTTP Post Test</h1>
  <p>
    Use the form below to send a test message and/or a file to dlptest.com over
    plain HTTP. The server accepts the request and discards the body. No data
    is logged, stored, or forwarded. This is intended as a tripwire so your DLP
    can detect — and ideally block — sensitive content as it leaves the
    endpoint.
  </p>
  <p>
    Need TLS instead? Use the <a href="/https-post/">HTTPS Post test</a>.
  </p>

  <PostTestForm scheme="http" />

  <h2>What is an HTTP POST?</h2>
  <p>
    HTTP POST is one of the request methods supported by the HTTP protocol. By
    design, a POST asks a server to accept the data enclosed in the body of the
    request, most often so it can store or process it. POSTs are how browsers
    upload files and submit forms.
  </p>
  <p>
    On dlptest.com we don’t do either — we accept the request, read enough of
    the body to satisfy the client, then drop it. Other sites will not.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
